{"shortDescription":"Redfin agents say pricing realistically from the start is the key to finding a buyer; 21% of home sellers are dropping their priceSEATTLE, Sept. 10, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Homebuying costs have hit their highest level in over a year, according to a new report from Redfin, the real estate brokerage po…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"i","children":["Redfin agents say pricing realistically from the start is the key to finding a buyer; 21% of home sellers are dropping their price"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["SEATTLE, Sept. 10, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Homebuying costs have hit their highest level in over a year, according to a new ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://edge.prnewswire.com/c/link/?t=0\u0026l=en\u0026o=4771025-1\u0026h=2748886641\u0026u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.redfin.com%2Fnews%2Fhousing-market-update-high-costs-sideline-buyers-negotiating-power\u0026a=report","linkText":"report"}}," from ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://edge.prnewswire.com/c/link/?t=0\u0026l=en\u0026o=4771025-1\u0026h=3865180557\u0026u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.redfin.com%2F\u0026a=Redfin","linkText":"Redfin"}},", the real estate brokerage powered by Rocket."]},{"type":"p","children":["Here's what else is happening in the housing market for the four weeks ending Sept. 6:"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["The typical U.S. homebuyer's monthly mortgage payment reached a 14-month high of $2,641"]},". That's partly because the median home-sale price rose 2.2% year over year, and partly because the weekly average mortgage rate increased to 6.71%."]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Elevated costs are keeping some would-be buyers on the sidelines."]}," Pending home sales were essentially flat (+0.1%) from a week earlier on a seasonally adjusted basis, sitting near their lowest level since February. Economic ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://edge.prnewswire.com/c/link/?t=0\u0026l=en\u0026o=4771025-1\u0026h=2942430253\u0026u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.redfin.com%2Fnews%2Fweekly-economic-update-september-8%2F\u0026a=uncertainty","linkText":"uncertainty"}}," is also contributing to sluggish demand. Buyers have negotiating power in most of the country, but for many house hunters, that isn't enough to offset high costs."]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["New listings fell due to Labor Day, but they're still higher than last year."]}," New listings fell 4.8% from a week earlier on a seasonally adjusted basis, but that's mostly because of the timing of Labor Day weekend. New listings are up 2.1% from a",{"type":"i","children":[" year"]}," ago, and the ",{"type":"i","children":["total"]}," number of homes for sale is also up 2.1%. Sellers are listing their homes because they want to sell before prices decline, life circumstances are prompting them to move, and the lock-in effect is easing."]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Sellers should adjust their expectations."]}," Just over one in five (20.8%) home listings had a price drop, up from 19.8% a year ago, and the typical home that sold spent 46 days on the market—one day longer than a year earlier. With some buyers shying away due to high costs and homes taking longer to sell, pricing a home realistically from the start is crucial. \"Pricing attracts attention. Overpricing creates hesitation,\" says Vanessa Leimback, a Redfin Premier agent in Seattle."]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"b","children":["But some homes are still attracting competition."]}," One-quarter (25.5%) of homes that sold went for over their asking price, up slightly from 24.9% a year earlier. Some parts of the country, including San Francisco and New York City suburbs, have competitive markets, and Redfin agents all over the U.S. say well-priced homes in desirable neighborhoods are still attracting bidding wars."]}]},{"type":"p","children":["For Redfin economists' takes on the housing market, please visit Redfin's \"From Our Economists\" page."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Leading indicators"]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":5,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Indicators of homebuying demand and activity"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Value (if applicable)"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Recent change"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Year-over-yearchange"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Source"]}]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Daily average 30-year fixed mortgage rate"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["6.97% (Sept. 9)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["Highest level in over a"]},{"type":"p","children":["year"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["Up from 6.29%"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["Mortgage News Daily"